                <pb facs="0660" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg562"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.918/53: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-04T14:00:00-05:00">March 4, 1930—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>82. Referring to Canton’s telegrams February 28, 1 p.m., and March 1, noon.
                    Department approves as appropriate under the circumstances action taken by the
                    American Consul General in reference to the reported desire of the Chinese
                    authorities to expel Lyon. Department asks that Legation reply to Canton’s
                    telegrams and report any further developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
